# tCrm — Cursor Rules

Internal CRM monorepo. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/rules.md`, `docs/design.md`, and `docs/inventory_and_logistics_flows.md` before making changes. When a change affects user-visible flows, update that flows doc in the same task (see `.cursor/rules/flows-documentation.mdc`).

## Stack

Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · TypeScript strict · Tailwind v4 · shadcn New York+zinc · MongoDB/Mongoose · Auth.js v5 · Turborepo/pnpm

## Key conventions

- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed
- Server Actions + `useActionState` for forms (not RHF)
- Co-locate `actions.ts` next to routes
- Models in `@crm/db`, auth in `@crm/auth`, shared utils in `@crm/lib`
- Always use `requirePermission()` in admin routes and mutations
- Wrap pages in `<Container>` from `@crm/ui`
- List views → `DataTable` (`tableId` required); panels → `EntitySheet` (not inline Cards above tables). Server pages use a client `*-table.tsx` wrapper — never pass `rowHref`, `rowDetail`, or column `render` from RSC (see `.cursor/rules/datatable.mdc`)
- Use semantic Tailwind tokens, not raw colors

## Workspace packages

`@crm/auth` `@crm/db` `@crm/lib` `@crm/ui` `@crm/core` — never import across `apps/*`

## Phase 0 scope

Foundation only: auth shell, dynamic RBAC, admin permissions UI, dashboard. Inventory is Phase 1.
